{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovConventionSeparation","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MarkovConventionSeparation","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Sqrt"],"declarations":13,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.markovZC_ne_markovZD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.markovZC_ne_markovZD","kind":"theorem","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MarkovConventionSeparation.lean#L136-L143","doc":"**Corollary for the migration.** At any substrate point above `q = 1` the\ntwo conventions are unequal, so a file that defines its Markov parameter through\nthe kernel is convention C and stays convention C however it is instantiated. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.markovZD_eq_sq_mul_kernel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.markovZD_eq_sq_mul_kernel","kind":"theorem","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MarkovConventionSeparation.lean#L129-L134","doc":"Convention D is the kernel at `q`, **rescaled by `q²`** — a different\nconstruction, not a different argument. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.markovZC_eq_kernel_sqrt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.markovZC_eq_kernel_sqrt","kind":"theorem","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MarkovConventionSeparation.lean#L123-L127","doc":"Convention C **is** the kernel evaluated at `√q` — the exact statement of\nwhat the Tier-2 generic form is, for `0 ≤ q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.markovZC_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.markovZC_one","kind":"theorem","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MarkovConventionSeparation.lean#L120-L121","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.markovZD_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.markovZD_one","kind":"theorem","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MarkovConventionSeparation.lean#L116-L118","doc":"The two conventions agree at `q = 1`, both equal to `1/2`: the classical\ncoincidence, and by the theorem above the only point of contact. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.no_kernel_instantiation_is_conventionD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.no_kernel_instantiation_is_conventionD","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MarkovConventionSeparation.lean#L105-L114","doc":"**The separation.** For `q > 1` no real `u` whatsoever sends the kernel to\nconvention D — so D is outside the kernel's range, not merely at a different\npoint of it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.half_lt_markovZD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.half_lt_markovZD","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MarkovConventionSeparation.lean#L98-L103","doc":"**Convention D exceeds `1/2` for every `q > 1`.**\n`z_D q - 1/2` has numerator `(q - 1) * (2q² + q + 1)`, and the second factor is\npositive for every real `q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.neg_half_le_markovKernel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.neg_half_le_markovKernel","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MarkovConventionSeparation.lean#L93-L96","doc":"The kernel is bounded below by `-1/2`, so its real range is `[-1/2, 1/2]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.markovKernel_le_half","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.markovKernel_le_half","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MarkovConventionSeparation.lean#L88-L91","doc":"**The kernel is bounded above by `1/2`.** Immediate from `0 ≤ (u - 1)²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.sq_add_one_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.sq_add_one_pos","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MarkovConventionSeparation.lean#L85-L86","doc":"The denominator never vanishes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.markovZC","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.markovZC","kind":"def","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MarkovConventionSeparation.lean#L82-L83","doc":"Convention **C**, excised. Kept here only as the object being separated. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.markovZD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.markovZD","kind":"def","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MarkovConventionSeparation.lean#L79-L80","doc":"Convention **D**, the canonical one (owner ruling R1, 2026-08-15). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.markovKernel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.markovKernel","kind":"def","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/MarkovConventionSeparation.lean#L64-L77","doc":"The rational kernel both conventions are built from: `g u = u / (u² + 1)`.\nThis is the generic Tier-2 `markovZ`, stated here over `ℝ` because the whole\npoint of this file is an inequality.\n\n**This is a convention-C object, deliberately, and it is here for comparison\nonly** — it is the thing convention D is separated *from*, and every theorem\nbelow is about the gap between it and `markovZD`. Do not consume it as a Markov\nparameter; `markovZD` is canonical (owner ruling R1, 2026-08-15).\n\nRecorded because `scripts/lean-markov-convention-audit.py` flagged this very\ndeclaration as actionable C on the run right after it was written — correct by\nits rules, and the right fix is for the site to announce itself rather than for\nthe detector to special-case a filename. ","signatureChunk":0}]}